        "conclusion": "violated",
        "defect_claim": "asserted",
        "rationale": "Receipt f5cb1459db5e418d9a9aa6987ef76dfc (exit 0, fourteen events, no parse loss) settles both comparisons of this question. Comparison 0 is violated by witness event index 11: after restarting the single-voter node with RestoreCommittedLogs on and no snapshot, became_leader is false and the final state is Follower across the whole 1500 ms sampling window, with after_latest_index 0 and the matching admission event recording before_latest_index 1 with one server. Comparison 1 holds at evaluated event index 13: the identical restart without the flag reported became_leader true, final state Leader and after_latest_index 1, so the difference tracks the recovery flag rather than restart timing. Source: with an empty latest configuration runFollower takes the 'no known peers, aborting election' branch and never sets Candidate (raft.go:228-232); even on the candidate path quorumSize() would be one while electSelf asks only the servers in that same empty list (raft.go:1087-1094, 1999-2060); and the configuration is empty because restoreFromCommittedLogs advanced lastApplied past the committed LogConfiguration before the startup scan (api.go:604-620, 724-754). Consequence under the witnessed conditions: a single-voter cluster that restarts with this flag never regains a leader, so duties needing a leader stay pending with no enabled path to completion, since the node's own committed log holds the configuration it would need. The multi-voter variant of the same question was later witnessed under the child question: with a five-voter committed configuration a restarted node kept the stale three-voter configuration and won leadership on two of the committed five votes (receipt abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407, violated at witness event index 22, control holding at 25), so the authority loss is not confined to an empty configuration.",
        "answers": {},
        "knowledge": [],
        "counterevidence": [
          "The flag-off control reaches Leader inside the same 1500 ms window, so the non-campaigning is not a general restart delay.",
          "The library deliberately grants votes when the server list is empty (a bootstrap affordance), which explains why such a node still answers vote requests; the witnessed defect is the state it resumes with, not the vote-granting rule."
        ],
        "limitations": [
          "This question's own witness is a single-voter configuration with no snapshot; the stale multi-voter election is witnessed under the child question and cited there, not re-observed here.",
          "The window is bounded at 1500 ms against a 50 ms election timeout, so a much later recovery is not excluded.",
          "The snapshot-age configuration variant is witnessed through the configuration observation and the child's election, not through this authority sample."
        ],
        "joint_history": "Receipt f5cb1459db5e418d9a9aa6987ef76dfc is this question's own execution (single-voter node, no snapshot, wall-clock sampling of the restarted node). Receipt abfdbd1823b342409ef4a815bade0407 belongs to the child multi-voter question and is cited here only for the follow-on statement that the authority loss also occurs with a stale non-empty configuration. The two are complete executions of different scenarios rather than fragments of one history, and neither is used to establish the other's comparison.",
