      "scope": {
        "description": "Five-voter cluster whose leading node is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs after a snapshot predating the membership change, isolated with one committed voter immediately after the restart; both sides acknowledge a distinct client write, the partition heals, and after eight seconds the event reports whether the two nodes' logs hold different entries at the same index, whether either node applied an entry absent from its own log, and the leadership and acknowledgement outcomes. Run with the flag on and off.",
        "assumptions": [
          "A successful Apply is an acknowledgement to the client.",
          "Two nodes holding different entries at the same log index after healing is a violation of log agreement.",
          "Eight seconds is enough for AppendEntries exchange between the two sides."
        ],
        "excluded": [
